```java
@Service
public class ReviewService {
    public static final String STAGE_LANGUAGE = "LANGUAGE";
    public static final String STAGE_COMPLIANCE = "COMPLIANCE";
    public static final String DECISION_APPROVE = "APPROVE";
    public static final String DECISION_REJECT = "REJECT";
    // statuses
    public static final String STATUS_PENDING = "PENDING";
    public static final String STATUS_BLOCKED = "BLOCKED";
    public static final String STATUS_PASSED = "PASSED";
```

Methods:
- configurePolicy(documentId, language, request): lock document, normalize language, check in target languages, expectedPolicyVersion vs current (default 0) → 409; validate stages (distinct reviewers, quorum <= size); insert policy version current+1, stages, reviewers, upsert current; bump draft version; return response.
- castVote(documentId, segmentId, language, actorId, request): lock document; normalize language; parse stage/decision; find segment (404), translation (404); active policy → else 422; policyVersion match → 422; stage config from listReviewStages; reviewer in candidates → 422; versions match (source/translation/term) → 422; other-stage vote check → 422; voteKey check → 409; latest vote → expectedVoteVersion check → 409; insert vote with voteVersion = current+1; catch DuplicateKeyException → 409 (voteKey race). Return response.
- getReviewMatrix(documentId): read-only; for each segment × targetLanguage: policyVersion (0 if none); if policy active: for each stage config compute counts from listLatestVotes filtered by current versions.
- getVoteHistory(documentId, segmentId, language): read-only; list votes; compute current (max version per reviewer+stage) and counting flags.
- verifyReviewGate(document, segments, translations): called from TranslationService.publish; returns Map<key, List<VoteRow>> of counting votes to freeze per segment+language (only for languages with active policy). Throws 422 if any stage not PASSED.

Stage evaluation helper:
```java
record StageEvaluation(String status, List<VoteRow> counting, int approveCount, int rejectCount, List<String> approvers, List<String> rejecters)
static StageEvaluation evaluate(List<VoteRow> latestVotes, int quorum, int sourceVersion, int translationVersion, int termVersion, int policyVersion)
```
counting = votes matching all versions. rejects among counting → BLOCKED. approveCount >= quorum → PASSED else PENDING.

For configurePolicy validation: reviewers distinct (422 if dup), quorum >= 1 (bean validation), quorum <= reviewers.size() → 422.

Draft version bump on policy configure: need repository.updateDraftVersion — exists.

Note: TranslationService.lockDocument is private; ReviewService will use repository.findDocumentForUpdate directly.

For castVote, termVersion check: vote.termVersion must equal document.termVersion().

Also voteKey uniqueness check: repository.findVoteByKey → if present throw 409. Then insert; catch DuplicateKeyException → 409.

Now matrix entry translationVersion: Integer (null if no translation). When no translation, stage evaluation: no votes can count (translationVersion unknown) — but votes require translation to exist, so if translation missing there are no votes; evaluation with translationVersion = -1 → nothing counts → PENDING. Fine.

getVoteHistory: for each vote, current = (vote_version == max for its reviewer/stage/segment/language group); counting = current && versions match current doc/segment/translation/policy versions. Need current versions per segment/language: load segments, translations, current policies, document.

Write ReviewService now.

